## Context

Exp2 produces `.md` narrative outputs (one per agent × arm × run) that contain
a structured inventory table (columns: Source 1, Source 2, Notes, plus the body
rows) and optionally an annotated bibliography section.  We want to measure how
well agents comply with the source-quality rules defined in the metaprompt, by
counting three tiers of reference quality for each field:

- **Empty** — cell blank or a bare null marker (`—`, `N/A`) with no attempt
- **Not-found** — agent explicitly wrote `not found` or `URL not verified`:
  tried to source, failed, declared it honestly (the metaprompt requires this)
- **Present** — cell has a substantive reference (not empty, not not-found)
- **Valid** — reference resolves: bibliography key found in the bibliography
  section (key-ref style: OpenAI, Anthropic); or URL returns HTTP 200 (for
  bibliography entries); NA for inline-ref style agents (Mistral, Qwen) where
  no resolvable key exists
- **Primary** — source classified as primary per the metaprompt taxonomy:
  official government documents, regulator-aggregated data, operator
  filings/press releases (e.g. `*.gov.vn`, `evn.com.vn`, `pvpower.vn`,
  `genco3.com`, named annual reports)

The metaprompt explicitly requires that tertiary/inadmissible sources appear
in Notes only, not in Source 1/2.  So `notes_present` is a compliance signal:
a well-behaved optimised-arm agent writes Notes when it found something only
via a tertiary source it could not trace to a primary.

Two citation styles co-exist **per run** (not per agent — same agent
switches across reps):
- **Key-reference**: Source 1/2 contain labels (`B05`, `B17`) that reference
  a bibliography section with URLs.  Observed: Anthropic 2/5, OpenAI 2/5.
- **Inline-reference**: Source 1/2 contain document descriptions
  (`EVN AR2023 p.44`, `MOIT PSR2021`); may or may not have a bibliography.
  Observed: all Mistral, all Qwen, Anthropic 3/5, OpenAI 3/5, all naive arm.

For inline-ref runs, `src_valid = NA` (no key to resolve), but `src_primary`
is still assessable from the document description alone.

The naive-arm prompt contains no source-quality section, so naive-arm agents
received no taxonomy guidance.  Comparing arms on these metrics therefore
measures the effect of the sourcing scaffold, not just agent capability.

## Relevant files

- `experiments/outputs/sota_exp2_brerun1/*.md` — optimised arm narratives (4 agents × 5 runs, canonical)
- `experiments/outputs/sota_exp2_naive_arm/*.md` — naive arm narratives (4 agents × 5 runs)
- NOTE: `sota_exp2_phase_b_full/` is excluded (weak classifier, per `tabulate_exp2_arms_runs.py`)
- `experiments/sota/protocol_02_metaprompt.md` — source-quality taxonomy (Primary / Secondary / Tertiary)
- `experiments/sota/protocol_07_naive_prompt.md` — naive arm prompt (no source-quality section)
- `src/aedist/plot_exp2_arms_comparison.py` — existing three-panel figure; this ticket adds a companion table
- `report/inputs/generated/tab_exp2_arms_runs.csv` — existing per-run metrics CSV; new columns should be added here or in a parallel CSV

## Actions

1. Write `src/aedist/extract_exp2_bib.py` — parser that reads a single `.md`
   file and returns a dict with:
   - `n_rows`: inventory table row count (data rows only)
   - `src1_empty`, `src1_notfound`, `src1_present`: counts (mutually
     exclusive, sum to `n_rows`); same for `src2`, `notes`
   - `src1_valid`, `src2_valid`: counts (NA string for inline-ref style)
   - `src1_primary`, `src2_primary`: counts (rule-based classifier, LLM
     fallback for ambiguous domains)
   - `bib_entries`: total entries in bibliography section
   - `bib_valid`: URL-200 count (async HTTP HEAD, 1 s per-host rate limit,
     5 s timeout); may be deferred to a separate `--validate-urls` flag
   - `bib_primary`: count of primary-tier entries
   - `citation_style`: `"key-ref"` or `"inline-ref"` (auto-detected)

2. Write a CLI driver that runs the parser over all 40 `.md` files and emits
   `report/inputs/generated/tab_exp2_bib_quality.csv` with columns:
   `agent, arm, run, n_rows,
    src1_empty, src1_notfound, src1_present, src1_valid, src1_primary,
    src2_empty, src2_notfound, src2_present, src2_valid, src2_primary,
    notes_empty, notes_notfound, notes_present,
    bib_entries, bib_valid, bib_primary, citation_style`

3. Wire a Makefile target: `report/inputs/generated/tab_exp2_bib_quality.csv`
   depending on the two `.md` glob sets and the script.

4. Write `src/aedist/tab_exp2_bib_quality.py` — render the CSV as a LaTeX
   table (one row per agent × arm, aggregated mean ± range across runs) and
   emit `report/inputs/generated/tab_exp2_bib_quality.tex`.

5. Add the `\input` to the appropriate report section.

## Test

```python
# tests/test_extract_exp2_bib.py

def test_openai_run01_key_ref_style():
    from aedist.extract_exp2_bib import parse_md
    result = parse_md(Path("experiments/outputs/sota_exp2_brerun1/openai_run02.md"))
    assert result["citation_style"] == "key-ref"
    assert result["src1_present"] >= 50   # most rows have Source 1
    # empty + notfound + present must sum to n_rows
    assert (result["src1_empty"] + result["src1_notfound"] +
            result["src1_present"]) == result["n_rows"]
    assert result["bib_entries"] >= 20
    assert result["src1_valid"] <= result["src1_present"]  # valid ⊆ present

def test_qwen_run01_inline_ref_style():
    from aedist.extract_exp2_bib import parse_md
    result = parse_md(Path("experiments/outputs/sota_exp2_brerun1/qwen_run01.md"))
    assert result["citation_style"] == "inline-ref"
    assert result["src1_valid"] is None   # NA for inline-ref
    assert result["src1_primary"] >= 0   # still classifiable from title

def test_anthropic_no_bib_run():
    from aedist.extract_exp2_bib import parse_md
    result = parse_md(Path("experiments/outputs/sota_exp2_brerun1/anthropic_run03.md"))
    assert result["bib_entries"] == 0
    # src1_valid = 0 or None depending on style detected
```

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `tab_exp2_bib_quality.csv` produced for all 40 runs (20 optimised + 20
  naive), no missing rows; `empty + notfound + present == n_rows` for every
  row in the CSV (enforced by an assertion in the parser)
- [ ] Citation style auto-detected correctly for all four agents
- [ ] `src_primary` classifier uses the three-tier taxonomy from
  `protocol_02_metaprompt.md` verbatim; domain list documented in the script
- [ ] Makefile target is up-to-date (running `make` twice produces no rebuild)
- [ ] LaTeX table renders without errors via `tectonic`
- [ ] `make check-fast` passes
